# `val s = "a ${n + 1} b"` - the construct `Maps.kt` does not contain once.
#
# Extents are read off the source text, not off any parser: `"a ${n + 1} b"`
# begins at byte 18 and `n + 1` at byte 23. `_string_start`, `_string_end` and
# `_interpolation_expression_start` are hidden, so the visible shape the
# grammar promises is string_literal > interpolated_expression.
#
# `lacks lambda_literal` is the discriminator against the shape this tree
# builds today: a blind scanner hands `${` to the ordinary lexer, which reads
# it as a brace and returns a lambda. That is a confidently wrong node, which
# the troupe contract calls worse than an unanswered token.
roots 1
mends 0
holds string_literal
holds interpolated_expression
lacks lambda_literal
spans string_literal 18 32
spans interpolated_expression 23 28
